<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harshacharita</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Harshacharita ('Deeds of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harsha">Harsha</a>') is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> prose biography of Harsha, king of Thanesar and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannauj">Kannauj</a>, written by his court poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banabhatta">Banabhatta</a> in the 7th century. In eight chapters it tells of the poet's own life, the Pushyabhuti family, the deaths of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prabhakaravardhana">Prabhakaravardhana</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajyavardhana">Rajyavardhana</a> and Harsha's early campaigns, breaking off before his later reign. It is among the first historical biographies in Sanskrit literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harshacharita.jpg" alt="Harshacharita" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original work by Banabhatta [Bāṇabhaṭṭa], unknown scribe · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Folio_of_a_manuscript_of_the_Harshacharita_by_Banabhatta,_written_in_Sharada_script.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
